# A bot folder is a plain (BotCorp-gitignored) folder, not a repo. This file
# matters only when the optional `backup:` module turns it into one
# (`botcorp backup <bot>` runs `git init` here and commits backup.paths); it
# then keeps the vault, the config home and the generated config out of the
# backup remote. `botcorp export` uses its own exclusion list.

# Runtime / editable Claude Code state (re-creatable; not the generated config)
.claude-*/
.claude/stash/
.claude/.current_session_id
.claude/.botcorp_*

# Generated by `botcorp sync` from bot.yaml (carries this machine's paths);
# `sync` rebuilds it, so it never travels. bot.yaml and settings.local.json do.
.claude/settings.json

# Secrets / vault
.vault/
.env
*.oauth_token
credentials.json
token.json

# Memory internals that are per-machine, not portable content
memory/index/
memory/tg/
memory/metrics/

# Misc
*.lock
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
